@startuml domain-ledger
title Ledger facts, balance queries and money

top to bottom direction
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam titleFontSize 22
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam classBorderColor #64748B
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classBackgroundColor<<ValueObject>> #DCFCE7
skinparam classBackgroundColor<<ReadModel>> #FEF3C7
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 40

interface LedgerReadPort {
  +getWalletBalance(walletId)\n  : Promise<WalletBalance | null>
  +getHoldingAccountBalance(accountId)\n  : Promise<HoldingAccountBalance | null>
}

interface WalletBalance <<ReadModel>> {
  +walletId : UUID
  +availableBalance : Money
}

interface HoldingAccountBalance <<ReadModel>> {
  +accountId : UUID
  +heldBalance : Money
}

class HoldingAccount <<Identity>> {
  +accountId : UUID
}

class LedgerTransaction <<ImmutableFact>> {
  +transactionId : UUID
  +amount : Money
  +kind : TransactionKind
  +occurredAt : Date
  +idempotencyKey : string
  +walletId : UUID [0..1]
  +holdId : UUID [0..1]
  +payoutId : UUID [0..1]
}

class Money <<ValueObject>> {
  {static} +fromCents(...) : Money
  +toCents() : number
  +add(...) : Money
  +subtract(...) : Money
  +multiply(...) : Money
  +divideFloor(...) : Money
}

LedgerReadPort .down.> WalletBalance : returns
LedgerReadPort .down.> HoldingAccountBalance : returns
HoldingAccountBalance -down-> HoldingAccount : accountId
LedgerTransaction -down-> Money : amount
LedgerReadPort -[hidden]right- LedgerTransaction
WalletBalance -[hidden]right- HoldingAccountBalance
HoldingAccountBalance -[hidden]right- Money

caption Selected public members; (...) abbreviates parameters.\nTransaction IDs refer to Wallet, FundHold and Payout. Wallet derives funds from its complete history.\nRead models serve independent queries; unknown accounts return null. Money uses safe integer SGD cents.
@enduml
